        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>A <strong>rational expression</strong> is, roughly speaking, an algebraic expression that&#x27;s in the form of a fraction, or contains fractions.</p>",
            "readable_text": "A rational expression is, roughly speaking, an algebraic expression that's in the form of a fraction, or contains fractions.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To evaluate a rational expression like <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac 6 x]</span> for <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x=2,]</span> all we need to do is replace <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x]</span> with <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2]</span> in the above expression and simplify as much as possible.</p>",
            "readable_text": "To evaluate a rational expression like [MATH: \\dfrac 6 x] for [MATH: x=2,] all we need to do is replace [MATH: x] with [MATH: 2] in the above expression and simplify as much as possible.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (6)/(x) = (6)/(2) = 3]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: (6)/(x) = (6)/(2) = 3]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nA rational expression is, roughly speaking, an algebraic expression that's in the form of a fraction, or contains fractions.\n\nContent:\nTo evaluate a rational expression like [MATH: \\dfrac 6 x] for [MATH: x=2,] all we need to do is replace [MATH: x] with [MATH: 2] in the above expression and simplify as much as possible.\n\nContent:\n[MATH: (6)/(x) = (6)/(2) = 3]"
      },
