    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nA rational expression is, roughly speaking, an algebraic expression that's in the form of a fraction, or contains fractions.\n\nContent:\nTo evaluate a rational expression like [MATH: \\dfrac 6 x] for [MATH: x=2,] all we need to do is replace [MATH: x] with [MATH: 2] in the above expression and simplify as much as possible.\n\nContent:\n[MATH: (6)/(x) = (6)/(2) = 3]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Evaluating a Single Fraction\n\nExample Prompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: \\dfrac{x-2}{x+1}] for [MATH: x=5.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe replace [MATH: x] with [MATH: 5] in the expression and simplify as much as possible.\n\n[MATH: (x \u2212 2)/(x + 1)|=; (5 \u2212 2)/(5 + 1)|=; (3)/(6)|=; (1)/(2)]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: (4)/(x + 1)] for [MATH: x = 7.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 4]\nb. [MATH: (2)/(3)]\nc. [MATH: 2]\nd. [MATH: (1)/(2)]\ne. [MATH: (4)/(7)]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: (6x)/(5 \u2212 3x)] for [MATH: x = 5.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (3)/(2)]\nb. [MATH: \u2212 (3)/(2)]\nc. [MATH: 2]\nd. [MATH: 3]\ne. [MATH: \u2212 3]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Evaluating Expressions With Parentheses\n\nExample Prompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: \\dfrac{3(2a-1)}{2(3a+1)}] for [MATH: a=1.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe replace [MATH: a] with [MATH: 1] in the expression and simplify as much as possible.\n\n[MATH: (3(2a \u2212 1))/(2(3a + 1))|=; (3(2(1) \u2212 1))/(2(3(1) + 1))|=; (3(2 \u2212 1))/(2(3 + 1))|=; (3(1))/(2(4))|=; (3)/(8)]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: (3(6 \u2212 x))/(x + 1)] for [MATH: x = 2.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 2]\nb. [MATH: 1]\nc. [MATH: 4]\nd. [MATH: 8]\ne. [MATH: 3]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: (p + 5)/(2(4 \u2212 p))] for [MATH: p = \u2212 3.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (4)/(7)]\nb. [MATH: \u2212 (4)/(7)]\nc. [MATH: (3)/(7)]\nd. [MATH: 1]\ne. [MATH: (1)/(7)]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Evaluating a Sum or Difference\n\nExample Prompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: \\dfrac{1}{p} + \\dfrac{1}{2p}] for [MATH: p=4.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe replace [MATH: p] with [MATH: 4] in the expression and simplify as much as possible.\n\n[MATH: (1)/(p) + (1)/(2p)|=; (1)/(4) + (1)/(2 \u22c5 4)|=; (1)/(4) + (1)/(8)|=; (2)/(8) + (1)/(8)|=; (2 + 1)/(8)|=; (3)/(8)]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: (6)/(w) + (w)/(6)] for [MATH: w = 2.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (5)/(3)]\nb. [MATH: (3)/(8)]\nc. [MATH: (10)/(3)]\nd. [MATH: (13)/(3)]\ne. [MATH: (8)/(3)]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: (9r + 3)/(3r + 1) \u2212 2r] for [MATH: r = 3.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 3]\nb. [MATH: \u2212 3]\nc. [MATH: \u2212 9]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 18]\ne. [MATH: 9]\n\n---\n\nItem 11 \u2014 Example: Evaluating Expressions With Multiple Variables\n\nExample Prompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: \\dfrac{n-2}{m-1} + \\dfrac{2(m+1)}{n}] for [MATH: m=4] and [MATH: n=6.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe replace [MATH: m] with [MATH: 4] and [MATH: n] with [MATH: 6] in the expression and simplify as much as possible.\n\n[MATH: (n \u2212 2)/(m \u2212 1) + (2(m + 1))/(n)|=; (6 \u2212 2)/(4 \u2212 1) + (2(4 + 1))/(6)|=; (4)/(3) + (2(5))/(6)|=; (4)/(3) + (10)/(6)|=; (4)/(3) + (5)/(3)|=; (4 + 5)/(3)|=; (9)/(3)|=; 3]\n\n---\n\nItem 12 \u2014 Question 7\n\nPrompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: (24)/(xy) + (x)/(4y)] for [MATH: x = 2] and [MATH: y = 3.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (25)/(6)]\nb. [MATH: (26)/(5)]\nc. [MATH: (5)/(6)]\nd. [MATH: (13)/(4)]\ne. [MATH: \u2212 (6)/(7)]\n\n---\n\nItem 13 \u2014 Question 8\n\nPrompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: (2r)/(r + t) \u2212 (r)/(t)] if [MATH: r = 3] and [MATH: t = 2.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (1)/(5)]\nb. [MATH: (3)/(10)]\nc. [MATH: \u2212 (3)/(10)]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 (1)/(5)]\ne. [MATH: 1]"
